# E4 Target inventory active-message depth focused evidence

Date: 2026-10-06
Base revision: `7d400a1a7d003d4f172deb87c7ef64cc3af1e082`

Latest focused command (after the sum-overflow guard):
`./gradlew test --tests com.nereusstream.delay.ownership.TargetWorkerTargetInventoryTest --tests com.nereusstream.delay.scheduler.OpenTelemetryMetricExporterTest`

Result: `BUILD SUCCESSFUL`. `TargetWorkerTargetInventoryTest` reports 5 tests, 0 skipped/failures/errors; `OpenTelemetryMetricExporterTest` reports 1/1, 0 skipped/failures/errors. `./gradlew checkstyleTest` passed. A separate invocation selected `TargetQuotaGrantStoreTest.realOxiaOwnerTakeoverReopensTargetRootAndCompletesCloseGc`; it reported 1 skipped because `NEREUS_DELAY_OXIA_ENDPOINT` is not configured.

The real two-RocksDB inventory regression persists per-Target `TargetQuotaTotal.ACTIVE_MESSAGES` values on two Shards and observes a shared physical Target depth of `2 + 5 = 7` and another Target depth of `3`. The telemetry path uses one independently bounded point read per `(source Shard, Target)` after a complete inventory, then rechecks every source Store cut. A missing total, incomplete point read, or changed cut omits the depth sample and adds the number of unavailable Target samples to `TARGET_INVENTORY_ACTIVE_MESSAGE_DEPTH_UNAVAILABLE`; it does not reject an already completed inventory. No message, timeline, or head-prefix scan is used. The histogram has no Target/Shard attributes and reports the distribution of active payload-owner messages, including messages that are not currently ready heads. The per-Shard totals are summed without a cross-Shard atomic timestamp.

The incomplete-read, changed-cut, and cross-Shard sum-overflow regression verifies that depth telemetry can be unavailable while the inventory remains complete and no stale or unrepresentable depth histogram is emitted. `OpenTelemetryMetricExporterTest` verifies the depth histogram and unavailable counter values, units, and empty attributes. These tests exercise the persisted quota-total read and multi-Shard sum; they do not substitute for a real-source message lifecycle test or Host-loop integration.

Host-loop integration assertion was added to `TargetQuotaGrantStoreTest.realOxiaOwnerTakeoverReopensTargetRootAndCompletesCloseGc`, but this turn could not execute it. Dockerized command:
`NEREUS_DELAY_OXIA_CHECKOUT=/Users/liusinan/apps/ideaproject/nereusstream/oxia NEREUS_DELAY_E2E_GRADLE_USER_HOME=/Users/liusinan/.gradle bash e2e/run-oxia-real-service.sh`

Result: failed before Gradle tests while Docker attempted to pull `alpine:3.22`; `registry-1.docker.io` DNS lookup failed (`no such host`). This is an environment block, not a test failure or pass. Earlier successful Oxia Host-loop validation covers scan-page event export only and is recorded separately in `evidence/e4-target-inventory-scan-metrics-focused.log`.

Other checks: `./gradlew checkDocumentation` passed; `jq empty docs/ndip/NDIP-3/progress.json` and `git diff --check` passed. `./gradlew checkstyleMain` failed only on the two pre-existing 123-character lines `PersistentLaneScheduler.java:1327` and `TargetWorkerHostRuntime.java:377`; neither line was changed in this slice. E4 remains `IN_PROGRESS / PENDING_CENTRAL_VALIDATION`.

